<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul stock market closed for three days.</title>
<headline>Seoul stock market closed for three days.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's stock market will be closed from Thursday for the Chusok holidays and will reopen on Monday.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, the composite stock index closed 15.30 points higher at 793.21, led by blue chips.</p>
<p>Brokers said blue chips were in favour ahead of the expansion of foreign stock ownership from October 1 to 20 percent from 18 percent.</p>
<p>-- Yeom Yoon-jeong (822) 727 5647</p>
